{
    "background_story": "Helena was a brilliant inventor and tinkerer, known to her friends and family as a maker of extraordinary things. Growing up in a family of engineers, she was always fascinated by the way things worked and loved taking apart and reassembling gadgets. As she grew older, Helena's passion for making things only intensified. She spent countless hours in her workshop, crafting innovative prototypes and solving complex problems. Her big break came when she created a revolutionary new material that could purify water in developing communities. Helena's invention earned her international recognition and accolades, but more importantly, it improved the lives of thousands of people around the world. She continued to create and innovate, always pushing the boundaries of what was possible.",
